DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Changes Coming to Call Center Phone Menus
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Changes Coming to Call Center Phone Menus\nChanges Comi
 ng to Call Center Phone Menus\nOct 07\, 2026\nStarting on\nOctober 12\, 20
 26\n\, when the MIHMS upgrade goes live\, we are also changing how callers
  interact with and experience Provider Services and Member Services call c
 enter phone menus\, known as Interactive Voice Response (IVR). With the go
 al of increasing caller satisfaction\, these changes will provide a modern
 ized IVR experience with streamlined navigation\, clearer call flows\, and
  improved overall caller efficiency.\nIntelligent Contact Center - Gabby\n
 A virtual assistant\, called Gabby\, will replace traditional phone menus 
 by listening to what callers say to resolve simple inquiries.\nWhen unable
  to resolve an inquiry\, Gabby will pass the call reason and context to a 
 live agent.\nGabby can answer common provider questions 24/7\, with inform
 ation such as:\nVerifying member eligibility\nMore ways to search for clai
 ms information\nMore detailed provider enrollment status\nProviding the fi
 ve most recent payments\nPrior authorization information\nLibrary of FAQs 
 to assist callers with common questions\nFeature\nToday's IVR\nGabby\nHow 
 It Works\nPress-based phone tree the caller navigates before reaching an a
 gent\nConversational\, natural language\, Gabby navigates directly to the 
 right agent\nCustomer Experience\n"Press 1 for claims…"\nGabby asks “I
 ’m here to help – what are you calling about?”\nNavigation\nMulti-le
 vel menus\nFlexible\, understands caller intent\nSupport Hours\nBusiness h
 ours\nMore information is accessible 24/7\, live agents available during b
 usiness hours\nFor all information about the upcoming changes to MIHMS\, s
 ee the “HealthPAS Online Portal” section of the\nProvider Resources\np
 age. For any questions regarding what to expect with the MIHMS upgra
 de\, please contact Provider Services at 1-866-690-5585.\nhttps://www.main
 e.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/changes-coming-call-center-pho
 ne-menus-2026-10-07
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/changes-co
 ming-call-center-phone-menus-2026-10-07
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4e86645186ac7348@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261007T230347Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 104 Filing of Maine Tax Returns (PDF)
DESCRIPTION:18  DEPARTMENT OF ADMINISTRATIVE AND FINANCIAL SERVICES \n \n1
 25  MAINE REVENUE SERVICES \n \nChapter 104: FILING OF MAINE TAX RETURNS \
 n \n \nSUMMARY: This rule describes the requirements for filing certain Ma
 ine tax returns\, including \nmandatory electronic filing of certain Maine
  tax returns\, and requirements of software developers to \ndevelop Maine 
 tax return forms. \n \n \n \nOUTLINE OF CONTENTS: \n \n.01 Definitions \n.
 02 General filing requirements – individual income tax returns \n.03 Man
 datory participation \n.04 Request for waiver from mandatory participation
  \n.05 Penalties \n.06 Software specifications \n.07 Application date \n \
 n \n \n \n.01 Definitions.  As used in this rule\, unless the context othe
 rwise indicates or may otherwise require\, \nthe following terms have the 
 following meanings that shall apply throughout the rule. \n \nA. “Electr
 onic filing” or “Electronic data submission” means the submission of
  return or \ndocument information using a computer\, the internet\, or any
  other means of electronic \nsubmission of data in a manner prescribed by 
 the State Tax Assessor (“Assessor”) where \nthe return or document inf
 ormation is electronically accepted by the Assessor. \nSpecifications for 
 the manner of the transfer of data may be found on the Maine Tax \nPortal\
 , Maine Revenue Services (“MRS”) website\, or by contacting MRS. \n \n
 B. “Maine tax return” means any Maine tax return\, including\, but not
  limited to\, any \nschedule\, worksheet\, report\, application\, or form 
 for purposes of 36 M.R.S. § 193 \n(original or amended) for which MRS pro
 vides a program for electronic filing or \nelectronic data submission. \n 
 \nC. “Person”  means an individual\, firm\, partnership\, association\
 , society\, club\, corporation\, \nfinancial institution\, estate\, trust\
 , business trust\, receiver\, assignee\, or any other group or \ncombinati
 on acting as a unit\, other than the State or Federal Government or any po
 litical \nsubdivision or agency of either government. \n \nD. “Prepares
 ”  means completes Maine tax returns directly\nhttps://www.maine.gov/rev
 enue/sites/maine.gov.revenue/files/inline-files/Rule104_October_2026.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/revenue/sites/maine.gov.revenue/files/inline-fil
 es/Rule104_October_2026.pdf
